{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"0f7a36e8e70a5ae2b5dcbc8f5cc2708f54ebac87805aaad326891d8a83fc8c04","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion gate recovery","key_entities":["CompletionAgentStep.run","LLMUnavailableError","completion_recovery.py","_degrade_from_actionable_bank","bank_has_actionable_block","completion_verdict_assembly.py","assemble_deterministic_verdict","close_precheck","completion_banking.py","test_completion_outage_degrade_b39a.py","ADR 0040","deterministic_fallback"],"problem_keywords":["completion gate","retry-with-backoff","operator-actionable block","banked criteria","verdict-less failure","LLM outage","deterministic fallback","retryable error"],"propositions":["When a completion verifier hits a provider outage (LLMUnavailableError) after already banking an operator-actionable BLOCK (met=False, evidence_sufficient not False), it must finalize a deterministic FAIL verdict from the bank without further LLM calls instead of dying verdict-less.","A completion run with an empty criterion bank or only PASS/insufficiency entries that hits a provider outage must re-raise the exception unchanged to preserve the exit-11 retryable retry posture per ADR 0040.","The deterministic BLOCK verdict from banked progress must have certifiable=False so it cannot auto-close the ticket; operator decision is required.","The degrade mechanism is guarded so any fault (bank read error, unreadable ticket) falls through to re-raise the outage unchanged, introducing no new failure mode on the outage path."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787884408397729001,"uu